spec:
  grid: 13-17 rows x 14-18 cols
  background: 5 (gray) [observed]
  sprites:
    count: 4-5 hollow 3x3 squares (8 border pixels, center = bg)
    colors: each sprite a distinct non-bg, non-guide color
    placement: non-overlapping, min 1-cell gap between any two sprite bboxes
  guide:
    color: 7 (orange) [observed]; differs from bg and all sprite colors
    structure: sparse pixels lying exactly on the perimeter of their own bbox
    bbox: 5-10 rows x 6-8 cols; covers 35-60% of grid area
    fill: 40-65% of full perimeter cells are guide pixels; rest are bg gaps
    connectivity: 3-6 disconnected fragments (4-conn)
    all 4 sides of bbox carry at least 1 guide pixel
  selection: exactly 1 sprite bbox is fully contained inside guide bbox; others are fully outside
  selected_sprite: margins from guide bbox edge >= 0 on each side (>= 1 on at least 2 sides)
  output: 3x3 crop of the selected sprite (the hollow square)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H in [13,17], W in [14,18].
    2. Choose N in [4,5] distinct non-bg non-guide colors for sprites.
    3. Place guide bbox (r0,c0,r1,c1) with height 5-10, width 6-8. May touch grid edges.
    4. Pick one sprite color as the selected sprite. Place its 3x3 hollow square
       inside the guide bbox with >= 0 margin on each side.
    5. Scatter remaining N-1 sprites on the grid fully outside the guide bbox,
       with >= 1 cell gap between any two sprites (and from guide bbox).
    6. Generate sparse guide perimeter pixels: for each cell on the guide bbox
       boundary, include it with ~50% probability; ensure all 4 sides have >= 1
       pixel and total fill is 40-65% of perimeter. Exclude cells occupied by sprites.
    7. Fill everything else with bg=5.
